{{Quote|Well, I asked for a dozen T-85 X-wings with cloaking devices. Guess they got held up in transit.|Poe Dameron of the Resistance shortly before the Battle of Crait|<ref name="The Last Jedi novel">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: Expanded Edition]]''</ref>}}
The '''T-85 X-wing starfighter''', also known as the '''New Republic X-wing fighter''', was a next-generation model of the [[X-wing starfighter]] utilized by the [[New Republic Defense Fleet]] during the [[Cold War|rise]] of the [[First Order]]. The [[starfighter]] was later used by the [[Resistance navy|naval forces]] of the [[Resistance]] during its [[First Order-Resistance War|struggle]] against the First Order.

==Characteristics==
[[Incom-FreiTek Corporation]]'s T-85 [[X-wing starfighter]] was an advanced version of the old [[T-65B X-wing starfighter]]. The X-wings featured<ref name="Before" /> 4 [[5L9 fusial thrust engine]]s and were equipped with a Class 1 [[hyperdrive]]. The engines could reach speeds up to 1,300 [[Kilometer per hour|KPH]] and 120 [[Megalight per hour|MGLT]].<ref name="RSOWM" /> The craft was flown by 1 [[pilot]] with an onboard [[astromech droid]] for assistance. Additional systems included [[deflector shield]]s and [[sensor]]s.<ref name="Before" /> The craft featured a distinctive nose to hold advanced [[Carbanti]] sensors. The engines could reach an acceleration of 3,800 [[G (unit)|G]] and a sublight speed of 120 [[Megalight per hour|MGLT]]. The dimensions were length of 15.68 [[meter]]s (51 ft 5 in), width of 13.65 meters (44 ft 9 in), and height of 2.7 meters (8 ft 10 in).<ref name="RSOWM" />

For armament, they carried four [[KX14 laser cannon]]s on the [[S-foils]] which deployed in the classic "X"-shape.<ref name="The Recruit" /> Additional weapons included [[Krupx Munitions|Krupx]] [[MG7-B proton torpedo launcher]]s. The old magnetic [[flash suppressor]]s were removed as unnecessary, although some pilots added custom ones. The engines were improved, with greater [[fusial thrust engine]]s installed. Improved flight systems also gave more maneuverability.<ref name="RSOWM" /> The [[cockpit]] was placed near the rear, with a snub nose.<ref name="The Recruit" /> Targeting systems included [[Fabritech]] [[ANr 1.3 tracking computer]] with [[IN-630-B "Sightline" holographic imaging system]]. For defenses, it was equipped with a [[Chempat]] [[deflector shield generator]] and had an [[ejector seat]] and [[life support]] for the pilot. The starfighter carried one week of supplies. The cost was 220,000 [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]] new and 140,000 used.<ref name="RSOWM" />

Some craft were [[color]]ed gray with blue trim, and had the words "Republic Navy" written on their hulls in [[Aurebesh]].<ref name="Buckets List 1">{{BucketsList|UfR9pzgIdLU|#1.1: "The Recruit"|sw_url=video/buckets-list-the-recruit-star-wars-resistance}}</ref>

==History==
===New Republic use===
The T-85s were flown by the [[New Republic Defense Fleet]]<ref name="Before" /> in the decades after the [[Battle of Endor]].<ref name="TLJ VD" /> The impetus of their design came from [[Admiral]] [[Gial Ackbar]], who realized that the [[T-70 X-wing starfighter|T-70s]] were aging. He proposed that Incom-Freitek design the next generation more than two [[Standard decade|decades]] after the founding of the [[New Republic]]. They were deployed to defend space lanes from [[pirate]]s.<ref name="RSOWM" /> [[Commander]] [[Poe Dameron]] flew T-85 X-wings with the rest of [[Rapier Squadron]] while serving the Republic. At one point, the Rapiers were assigned to [[Brooksdion Station|Brooksdion]] [[space station]]. They received an alert, as unknown parties had stolen the head of [[Mathieson's protocol droid]]. They scrambled in their T-85s and gave chase to the [[Unidentified Resistance starship|starship]]. As they reached the [[asteroid field]] of [[Lost Souls]], Dameron ordered his wingmen to remain behind while he pursued the ship. After escaping the field, the starship was able to outsmart Dameron and escape into hyperspace.<ref name="AOR:Poe">[[Age of Resistance - Poe Dameron 1|''Age of Resistance - Poe Dameron'' 1]]</ref> On another mission, Rapier Squadron ambushed a [[pirate]] [[frigate]] in the [[Mirrin sector]]. Dameron's fighter was disabled with an ion pulse, and towed aboard the frigate. His droid [[BB-8]] was able to slip away, alerting the rest of the squadron to their location, and they arrived to confront the frigate. Dameron was then able to subdue the crew thanks to the distraction.<ref name="Kidnapped">{{IDWAdventuresCite-2017|issue=24|story=Kidnapped!}}</ref>

Following his actions at the [[Skirmish in OR-Kappa-2722]] and the [[Suraz engagement]], Dameron was subsequently recruited into the [[Resistance]],<ref name="Before" /> becoming the leader of [[Black Squadron (Resistance)|Black Squadron]]. He switched to the use of a T-70, ''[[Black One]]''.<ref name="Poe Dameron 1">[[Poe Dameron 1|''Poe Dameron'' 1]]</ref>

===First Order conflict===
[[File:XionosSquadron-TheRecruitPart1.png|thumb|left|250px|New Republic X-wings pursued by a First Order TIE/ba interceptor.]]
While on a mission from [[New Republic High Command|New Republic Command]], [[Kazuda Xiono]]'s [[Kazuda Xiono's team|team]] employed T-85s. They were sent to [[Mission to rendezvous with the Resistance|rendezvous]] with the Resistance to pass along intelligence. [[Major]] [[Elrik Vonreg]] of the [[First Order]] [[Starfighter combat|engaged]] them. Xiono ordered his wingmen to escape, but his craft was damaged. Commander Dameron's arrival at the site saved Xiono, allowing them to trap and damage [[Elrik Vonreg's TIE Interceptor|Vonreg's TIE]] with his sole remaining cannon, forcing him to retreat. Xiono's craft was then towed aboard a [[Unidentified CR90 corvette (Resistance)|CR90 corvette]].<ref name="The Recruit">{{Resistance|The Recruit}}</ref>

Most of<ref name="RSOWM" /> the New Republic's T-85 X-wing [[fleet]] was atomized when the [[First Order]] [[Hosnian Cataclysm|destroyed]] the [[Hosnian system]] in [[34 ABY]].<ref name="TLJ VD" /> Shortly afterward, Commander Dameron joked to General [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] that he had ordered a shipment of T-85s in the leadup to the [[Battle of Crait]] as the Resistance [[Battle of Oetchi|fled]] the First Order counter-attack.<ref name="The Last Jedi novel" />

Following the devastating losses at Crait, the Resistance was down to only a small amount of men and material. Meanwhile the First Order had begun large-scale scrapping of captured New Republic ships. General Organa ordered a team to the scrap planet [[Bracca]], and [[Shriv Suurgav]] led [[Dross Squadron]] to [[Mission to Bracca|recover]] several starships, including one T-85.<ref name="Resistance Reborn" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:T85-TheRecruitPart1.jpg|thumb|right|300px|A T-85 X-Wing]]
The T-85 X-wings first appeared in the [[2015]] young-readers novel ''[[Before the Awakening]]'', written by [[Greg Rucka]] and published as part of the ''[[Journey to Star Wars: The Force Awakens]]'' imprint, although it was visually depicted as Poe Dameron's ''Black One'', a T-70 model.<ref name="Before" /> Their full design was revealed in "[[The Recruit]]," the premiere of the ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'' animated television series<ref name="SWR release">{{SW|url=news/new-star-wars-resistance-extended-sneak-peek|text=Strap In for a New ''Star Wars Resistance'' Extended Sneak Peek}}</ref> that aired on [[October 7]], [[2018]].<ref name="SWR release">{{SW|url=news/new-star-wars-resistance-extended-sneak-peek|text=Strap In for a New ''Star Wars Resistance'' Extended Sneak Peek}}</ref> The full designation was provided in the [[Star Wars Starships & Vehicles 3|third issue]] of ''[[Star Wars Starships & Vehicles]]'', released in June [[2021]].<ref name="SWShips 3">[[Star Wars Starships & Vehicles 3|''Star Wars Starships & Vehicles'' 3]]</ref>

The illustrations featured in ''Before the Awakening'' incorrectly depict the T-85 X-wings as T-70s, which were set to prominently appear in the then-upcoming film {{Film|VII}}. According to the [[Lucasfilm Story Group]]'s [[Matt Martin]], the images were incorrect, but were not an accidental depiction because the ''Journey to Star Wars: The Force Awakens'' publishing program had aimed to invoke the feeling of the film, and also the T-85 X-wings had not been designed at that point.<ref name="Martin tweet">{{Twitter|missingwords|status/1058403172555751424|[[Matt Martin]]|quote=I don't know if 'erroneous' is exactly the word I'd use as that implies that it was a mistake but yeah, it's incorrect. [[Before the Awakening|BTA]] was a tie-in to [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|TFA]] so it needed to have images that invoke the feeling of that film... also T-85 designs just didn't exist yet.|archivefile=File:T-85_tweet.png}}</ref> This is also the case for ''[[Poe and the Missing Ship]]'', a [[2017]] partial storybook adaptation of the aforementioned novel.<ref name="PatMS">''[[Poe and the Missing Ship]]''</ref>

Although ''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: The Visual Dictionary]]''<ref name="TLJ VD" /> declared that all T-85s were destroyed, this was overwritten by later sources such as the novel ''[[Resistance Reborn]]''.<ref name="Resistance Reborn" />

